Q: Why flex items overflow the flex container? A: <pre class="lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>.email-form {
    box-sizing: content-box;
}
</code></pre>
<p>You set box-sizing: border-box globally with *, but then overrode it back to content-box on the form. With content-box, the form's width: 100% only accounts for the content area — padding and border are added on top of that — so the children end up wider than the container. Just remove the box-sizing: from .email-form class.</p>
